# A halving loop on a nat: x := x / 2 is integer division, so from x = 5 the loop runs three
# times (5, 2, 1, 0) and terminates with c = 3; the upper bound 0 on the expectation of c is
# false.
# Expected: unknown.  The bound checker works over the reals, and integer division has no real
# counterpart, so the problem is not relaxed and no answer is given.  Read with x a real, the
# loop never terminated, the expectation was 0, and the bound 0 held.
nat x;
nat c;
x := 5;
c := 0;
while (0 < x) {
	x := x / 2;
	c := c + 1;
}
?Ex [c] <= 0
